    "headline": "Red Flag Warning issued October 16 at 2:31AM PDT until October 16 at 10:00PM PDT by NWS Hanford CA",
    "description": "* AFFECTED AREA...Fire weather zone 592 Central Sierra.Fire\nweather zone 593 North Kings River.Fire weather zone 594\nSequoia Kings.Fire weather zone 595 Lake Isabella.\n\n* WIND...STRONG NORTHEAST WINDS EXPECTED. A 70 TO 90 PERCENT\nPROBABILITY OF GUSTS EXCEEDING 40 MPH ON THURSDAY. A 40 TO 60\nPERCENT PROBABILITY OF GUSTS EXCEEDING 40 MPH ON FRIDAY.\n\n* HUMIDITY...MINIMUM RELATIVE HUMIDITY BETWEEN 15-25 PERCENT\nBOTH DAYS.\n\n* THUNDERSTORMS...NO THUNDERSTORM THREAT.\n\n* HIGHEST THREAT...IS LOCATED FOR ELEVATIONS ABOVE 4,000 UP TO\nTHE CREST OF THE SIERRA NEVADA.\n\n* IMPACTS...ANY FIRES THAT DEVELOP WILL LIKELY SPREAD RAPIDLY.\nOUTDOOR BURNING IS NOT RECOMMENDED.",
    "instruction": "A Red Flag Warning means that critical fire weather conditions\nare either occurring now, or will shortly. A combination of\nstrong winds, low relative humidity, and warm temperatures can\ncontribute to extreme fire behavior.",
